WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.150
- [Zac] What lies beneath
the dark subconscious

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:03.870
of a faceless silent killer?

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.670
What is present behind the black eyes

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.300
of what was just a six-year-old child

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.390
on Halloween night in 1963?

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.970
One psychiatric doctor by
the name of Samuel Loomis

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.980
was prepared to find out
what goes bump in the night

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.676
within the mind of Haddonfield,
Illinois's boogeyman,

00:00:15.676 --> 00:00:16.910
Michael Myers.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.100
To learn the fate of Dr. Loomis's fiance

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.580
and how it might've changed
his entire life going forward,

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.471
stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:23.471 --> 00:00:26.804
(metal intro music)

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.400
Welcome to "Horror History."

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.240
In today's lesson, I am analyzing the man

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.820
who tried to understand
an incomprehensible evil.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.400
There are many versions of this character

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.970
because there are many alternate timelines

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.070
in the "Halloween" story.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:42.020
I like to think of the
timeline like a train map,

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.330
the "Halloween Express."

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:44.163
Today, I'll just be analyzing

00:00:44.163 --> 00:00:46.120
the original timeline where Dr. Loomis

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.090
is portrayed by actor Donald Pleasence.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.550
There may be other videos where we ride

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.339
the Halloween Express
down alternate routes.

00:00:51.339 --> 00:00:53.470
If you want to make
things more complicated,

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.480
there is a theory that
the character Sam Loomis

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.540
in "Psycho" is the very same Sam Loomis

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:59.050
as the one in the "Halloween" series.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.300
Sam Loomis in "Psycho"
follows a private investigator

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.230
to find his missing
girlfriend, Marion Crane.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:04.201
But before Sam can find her,

00:01:04.201 --> 00:01:07.400
she's already dead alongside
the private investigator.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.492
This theory says that Sam
was driven to the obsession

00:01:09.492 --> 00:01:11.410
of learning how the criminal mind works,

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.670
which leads him to take the
job at Smith's Grove Sanitarium

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:14.640
where he meets Michael.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.032
As much fun as that idea is,

00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:18.220
personally, I think "Halloween" Sam Loomis

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.200
was just named after "Psycho" Sam Loomis

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:22.290
because director John
Carpenter was paying homage

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.640
to a great movie that
inspired the slasher genre.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.969
In order for me to turn
Dr. Loomis's psychoanalysis

00:01:26.969 --> 00:01:28.920
back at him, I'm going to take it back

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.601
to his first appearance in the franchise.

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:33.268
(ominous music)

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:38.670
Dr. Samuel Loomis began
his psychological studies

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:41.460
of the feared Michael Myers
on November 5th, 1963,

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:42.350
when Michael was admitted

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.850
to Smith's Grove Sanitarium.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:45.920
Michael was silent and
unmoving after the murder

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.070
of his sister, Judith Myers.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:49.100
Dr. Loomis seemed to think
that he was experiencing

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.845
severe trauma and damage
to a psychological health.

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:54.018
He opted for specialized
treatment to try to penetrate

00:01:54.018 --> 00:01:56.840
through Michael's unwavering
lack of emotional response.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.680
The early months of
Loomis's care for Michael

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.464
are mostly a mystery
because this time period

00:02:00.464 --> 00:02:02.600
is never covered in the Halloween canon.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:05.251
However, if we look at the
non-canon Chaos Comics material,

00:02:05.251 --> 00:02:07.440
we can get a little bit more backstory.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.990
This is one of those cases where the comic

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:10.275
doesn't contradict anything in the movies,

00:02:10.275 --> 00:02:12.277
and it can potentially
help us understand Loomis

00:02:12.277 --> 00:02:14.500
a little bit better, so I'm kind of okay

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.400
with talking about it,

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.643
as long as we remember that
this technically doesn't count.

00:02:17.643 --> 00:02:19.818
Loomis requested his
supervisor, Dr. Carpenter,

00:02:19.818 --> 00:02:22.360
to move Michael into a
private room safely away

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.635
from the other juveniles of the building.

00:02:23.635 --> 00:02:25.587
But Dr. Carpenter declined
to Loomis's request

00:02:25.587 --> 00:02:28.330
and kept Michael where he
was with the other juveniles.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:30.054
There was one other
doctor at the Sanitarium

00:02:30.054 --> 00:02:32.420
that saw Michael the
same way that Loomis did,

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.380
a woman by the name of Jennifer Hill.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.930
He asked her to speak with Dr. Carpenter

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.300
with him in order to convince him

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.700
that Michael needed to be moved.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.130
Dr. Hill did agree to do this

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:42.100
under the condition that
Loomis take her out to dinner.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.920
And although their attempt
to get Michael moved

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.208
to solitary was not successful,

00:02:45.208 --> 00:02:47.430
Dr. Hill's attempt at romance was,

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.609
and the two started dating, bonding

00:02:48.609 --> 00:02:51.060
over their shared beliefs
about psychotherapy.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.943
Over the next few months,
a few incidents took place

00:02:52.943 --> 00:02:54.890
with the other juveniles at the facility,

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:56.952
like Michael shoving a crayon
deep into the fellow patient

00:02:56.952 --> 00:02:58.032
Tony O'Malley's left eye.

00:02:58.032 --> 00:03:00.530
This was before security
cameras were common

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.210
so Loomis and the Smith's Grove staff

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:04.520
could not find any evidence
that Michael was responsible

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.260
and ended up blaming another child.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.184
In November, a child by
the name of Adrian Wade

00:03:08.184 --> 00:03:09.730
ate an entire birthday cake

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.060
that was supposed to be given to Michael.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:12.932
Shortly after, Adrian was
found in the shower room

00:03:12.932 --> 00:03:15.200
with second degree
burns all over his body.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.230
He later died in the
hospital of heart failure.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.090
After months of further study of Michael

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.270
and his psychological health,

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:21.660
Dr. Loomis started to believe

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.900
that the young Meyers boy
did not suffer from trauma

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.490
that occurred on Halloween 1963,

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:28.016
but found that behind his
eyes leaked only darkness.

00:03:28.016 --> 00:03:30.211
He had no conscience, no remorse,

00:03:30.211 --> 00:03:33.610
no response to the perception
of life, death, consequence,

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:34.610
or right and wrong.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:36.846
Only a psyche of pure evil.

00:03:36.846 --> 00:03:38.779
(eerie reel clicking)

00:03:38.779 --> 00:03:41.325
- I spent eight years trying to reach him

00:03:41.325 --> 00:03:44.360
and then another seven
trying to keep him locked up

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.060
because I realized that what was living

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:50.510
behind that boy's eyes was
purely and simply evil.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.926
- On May 1st, 1964, only
months after Michael

00:03:52.926 --> 00:03:55.000
was admitted to Smith's Grove Sanitarium,

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.050
Loomis met with two of the
lead doctors of the facility

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:59.280
to try to move Michael to
a maximum security ward

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.420
in Litchfield, Illinois.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.090
The two doctors refused
Loomis's suggestion

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:04.270
stating that Michael was
in a state of comatose

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:06.190
and did not react to
anything in his surroundings,

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:07.450
but Loomis did not agree.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:09.750
Loomis believed that Michael
was using the state of mind

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.640
to cover up his true dark behaviors

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.230
and insisted he'd be moved somewhere else

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.060
where it would be impossible
for him to escape.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.870
The doctors then gave Loomis a choice;

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:18.750
either Loomis would continue
working with Michael

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.170
at Smith's Grove or someone else

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:21.400
would be assigned to the patient.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.630
Loomis reluctantly agreed
to the doctors' terms

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:24.763
because he felt that no
one else could be trusted

00:04:24.763 --> 00:04:25.854
to work with him.

00:04:25.854 --> 00:04:28.240
It makes me wonder if things
could have gone differently

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.270
if another doctor had
worked closely with Michael.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:31.610
It seems like one of the main issues

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:33.480
was that most of the other
doctors didn't believe

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:35.690
that such a young boy
could be so full of evil.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.590
So it might've benefited
Loomis to have someone else

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.370
see the patient from his perspective.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:41.570
The only one who really kind
of understood the danger that

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:43.800
Michael posed was his
girlfriend, Dr. Hill.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.340
As the two continue to get closer,

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:46.640
they were eventually engaged

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:49.040
with a wedding planned for December 1971.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.277
However, disaster would strike

00:04:50.277 --> 00:04:51.784
before the big day would come.

00:04:51.784 --> 00:04:55.220
In October 1971, Dr. Carpenter
threw a Halloween party

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:56.610
at the Sanitarium, which Loomis

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:58.160
was heavily in opposition of.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.577
That night the electricity went out

00:04:59.577 --> 00:05:01.690
and a girl by the name
of Nancy was found dead,

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:03.559
drowned during a game
of Bobbing for Apples.

00:05:03.559 --> 00:05:05.670
The same night, Dr. Hill was found dead

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:06.741
outside of the Sanitarium.

00:05:06.741 --> 00:05:08.199
Her death was ruled a suicide

00:05:08.199 --> 00:05:10.270
because it seemed that she either fell out

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.800
or jumped off the roof of the building.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:12.846
But Loomis knew better.

00:05:12.846 --> 00:05:15.560
He knew in his gut that
Jennifer would not kill herself.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:16.730
And he couldn't see a scenario

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:19.070
that didn't involve Michael
getting his hands dirty.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:21.290
I think this was really
the last straw for him.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:23.630
Jennifer was the one person
that Loomis could connect to,

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:26.270
not only in terms of his
personal life, but also at work.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:27.520
She was the only other person

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.090
who could see Michael's true nature.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:30.596
I think this must be when he snapped

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:33.160
and made it his life's
goal to suppress the evil

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.890
lurking inside of the Sanitarium.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:36.685
For the next seven years, he did his best

00:05:36.685 --> 00:05:39.000
to keep Michael locked away from society.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.720
And this strategy worked
until the night of

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.676
October 30th, 1978, where
Michael escaped from captivity

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:46.285
to bring evil upon Haddonfield once again.

00:05:46.285 --> 00:05:48.952
(ominous music)

00:05:50.802 --> 00:05:53.885
(soft ominous music)

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.610
Loomis and his assistant,
Nurse Marion Chambers,

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:59.500
were given the assignment
of transporting Michael

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.471
from Smith's Grove Sanitarium

00:06:00.471 --> 00:06:02.860
to his home county of
Livingston for trial.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:05.640
The week prior, Michael had
turned 21 and was due in court

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.260
to see if he was fit to be released.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:08.670
On the drive up to Smith's Grove,

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.533
Loomis continually refers
to Michael as "it,"

00:06:10.533 --> 00:06:12.070
which Marion catches onto.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:15.360
- [Marion] Don't you think we
can refer to "it" as "him."

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:16.630
- If you say so.

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:18.560
- Here, Loomis shows that
he no longer sees Michael

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.930
as a human, but as an
embodiment of pure evil.

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:22.460
He suggests that Marion
should give Michael

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:23.921
a dose of Thorazine,
which is a strong drug

00:06:23.921 --> 00:06:25.513
used to control psychotic disorders,

00:06:25.513 --> 00:06:28.050
causing her to realize that
Loomis doesn't want Michael

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:29.627
to have any chance of winning his trial.

00:06:29.627 --> 00:06:31.220
As they get closer to the facility,

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:33.420
they noticed several of the
patients wandering the grounds

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:34.640
which strikes dread into him

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:36.540
because he fears that
Michael may have escaped.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.160
He runs up to the gates
to use the telephone,

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.170
trying to warn the staff,

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:40.700
when Michael jumps on the roof of the car

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.280
and grabs Marion through the window.

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:43.277
Loomis is unable to stop Michael,

00:06:43.277 --> 00:06:45.511
as he chases and out of
the car, gets inside,

00:06:45.511 --> 00:06:46.928
and frantically drives away.

00:06:46.928 --> 00:06:49.039
Strangely, Loomis
doesn't seem that shocked

00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:51.050
at Michael's ability to operate a car.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.549
Even though he'd been
locked up since age six

00:06:52.549 --> 00:06:54.670
and probably had never even been in a car

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:56.090
over the last 15 years.

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:58.177
His response all ties back
to the idea that Michael

00:06:58.177 --> 00:07:01.349
is no man, but rather just an
incarnation of evil itself.

00:07:01.349 --> 00:07:03.815
We're just seeing how
desensitized he has become to it.

00:07:03.815 --> 00:07:06.380
In fact, he already knows
Michael is on his way back

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:09.090
to Haddonfield for Halloween
and drives in that direction.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:10.912
On his way, he discovers
Michael's medical gown

00:07:10.912 --> 00:07:13.280
and the matchbook that Marion
had used the night before,

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.760
so he knows he's on the right track.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:17.070
He decides to investigate the
grave site of Judith Myers

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:18.930
only to find her headstone
has been removed,

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:21.280
confirming his suspicion
that Michael has come home.

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:22.820
After enlisting the help
of the local sheriff,

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:23.955
Leigh Brackett, the two checkout

00:07:23.955 --> 00:07:26.670
Michael's old residence at 45 Lampkin Lane

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:27.910
which has been broken into.

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:30.140
The two discover Michael's
first confirmed victim

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:32.230
of the evening, a dog
they found in the house.

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:34.880
See, I can kind of disagree
but sympathize with Michael

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.522
wanting to take out humans, but a dog?

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.111
That's just messed up man.

00:07:38.111 --> 00:07:39.390
Loomis convinces Sheriff Brackett

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:42.350
that Michael was probably
nearby and needs to be captured.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:44.410
It's here that we see
that despite his bravery

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:46.081
to try to spot Michael,
Loomis is terrified

00:07:46.081 --> 00:07:48.060
of Haddonfield's so-called boogeyman

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:49.780
and the capabilities that he possesses.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.320
Loomis eventually discovers
the stolen sanitarium vehicle

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.040
from the night before across the street.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.154
He walks the streets of Haddonfield

00:07:55.154 --> 00:07:56.500
until later that evening,

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:58.930
he sees two young kids running
out of a house screaming.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:00.710
Loomis is able to recognize their screams

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:03.839
as true terror, as opposed to
an innocent Halloween prank.

00:08:03.839 --> 00:08:05.022
(man yells)

00:08:05.022 --> 00:08:06.070
(group laughs)

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:07.990
And he runs into the
house to find 17-year old

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:09.890
Laurie Strode being strangled by Michael.

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:12.040
Laurie manages to pull
Michael's mask off for a moment,

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.122
giving Loomis time to shoot him.

00:08:13.122 --> 00:08:14.408
How many times Dr. Loomis?

00:08:14.408 --> 00:08:16.330
- [Sam] I shot him six times!

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.330
- [Zac] Which sends Michael
over the balcony railing

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.163
onto the lawn.

00:08:19.163 --> 00:08:20.460
By the time Loomis tends to Laurie

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:21.440
and looks over the balcony,

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:22.887
his former patient is no longer there.

00:08:22.887 --> 00:08:25.476
Michael had vanished and we
can visibly see how shaken up

00:08:25.476 --> 00:08:27.833
Dr. Loomis is by the
realization that his nemesis

00:08:27.833 --> 00:08:31.390
isn't just evil, inhuman, and
possibly the devil incarnate,

00:08:31.390 --> 00:08:32.636
but also invincible.

00:08:32.636 --> 00:08:33.918
Loomis looks out into the world

00:08:33.918 --> 00:08:35.660
wondering where Michael has gone next.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.140
The next door neighbor comes out

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:38.570
and helps Loomis get ahold of the police.

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:40.657
So the search continues
leading to this incident.

00:08:40.657 --> 00:08:43.082
(eerie reel clicking)

00:08:43.082 --> 00:08:46.276
(suspenseful music and
car tires screeching)

00:08:46.276 --> 00:08:48.610
(car explodes)

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:50.550
Sheriff Brackett asks if
this victim is Michael,

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:51.977
but before they find
out, Brackett is informed

00:08:51.977 --> 00:08:54.550
that his teenage daughter,
Annie, was found dead.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:56.060
Sheriff Brackett identified the body

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:58.200
and set off to tell his
wife of the circumstances,

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.068
which he blames on Loomis.

00:08:59.068 --> 00:09:01.270
That's gotta be crushing for Dr. Loomis.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:02.609
He tried to warn the psychiatric hospital

00:09:02.609 --> 00:09:04.769
how dangerous Michael was for 15 years,

00:09:04.769 --> 00:09:07.645
then he got away, Dr. Loomis's
worst nightmares came true

00:09:07.645 --> 00:09:08.894
despite his best efforts,

00:09:08.894 --> 00:09:11.040
and after all of that he still shoulders

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:12.060
the brunt of the blame.

00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:13.905
That kind of treatment
just makes a guy go.

00:09:13.905 --> 00:09:15.670
(Loomis yells)

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:17.190
Deputy Hunt would fill in for Brackett

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.220
from that point forward.

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.060
Hunt believes that the
crash victim is Michael,

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.580
which may have just been wishful thinking

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:22.812
because Loomis is not convinced.

00:09:22.812 --> 00:09:24.580
The dentist at the coroner's office

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.220
estimated the burned body from his teeth

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:27.296
to be about 17 years old,

00:09:27.296 --> 00:09:29.350
although a full check of dental records

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:30.203
would take hours to complete.

00:09:30.203 --> 00:09:32.470
I think some part of
Loomis knows that Michael

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:33.400
is still on the loose,

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.837
so he convinced Deputy Hunt to
a further patrol of the town.

00:09:35.837 --> 00:09:37.587
Loomis directs him back
to the Myers house,

00:09:37.587 --> 00:09:39.336
thinking that maybe if
Michael was injured,

00:09:39.336 --> 00:09:41.708
the familiarity of his old home
could have give him security

00:09:41.708 --> 00:09:42.756
in his vulnerable state.

00:09:42.756 --> 00:09:45.029
The house is already being swept by police

00:09:45.029 --> 00:09:47.513
while local townsfolk mob
outside and vandalize the place

00:09:47.513 --> 00:09:50.348
as some kind of weird post
tragedy form of protest.

00:09:50.348 --> 00:09:52.723
It's there that a pair of high
school boys express concern

00:09:52.723 --> 00:09:55.070
to Deputy Hunt because
their friend Bennett Tramer

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:57.120
didn't get home after
leaving a costume party.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.100
Hunt and Loomis both suspect the worst

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:00.750
that the burned body belonged to Tramer,

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:02.700
meaning that Myers must
still be out there.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.570
Before being able to
really put together a plan,

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:06.500
they're called to
Haddonfield Elementary school

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.090
where another break-in has taken place,

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:09.820
possibly their chance to catch Michael.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:11.403
They discover a child's
picture of a family

00:10:11.403 --> 00:10:14.150
decorated with a knife that
Michael has left piercing

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:15.010
the daughter's heart.

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:15.843
On the chalkboard,

00:10:15.843 --> 00:10:17.290
the word "Samhain" is written in red

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:19.488
and Loomis is the only one
that knows its Celtic origin.

00:10:19.488 --> 00:10:21.980
It's essentially an ancient
Gaelic festival of the dead

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:24.090
celebrating the end of summer
and the beginning of winter,

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:26.410
which began on what we now
know is Halloween night.

00:10:26.410 --> 00:10:27.920
They're interrupted by Nurse Chambers

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:29.520
who informs Dr. Loomis that the Governor

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.020
has ordered him to leave Haddonfield

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:33.280
under the belief that he's
contributing to the hysteria.

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:35.530
Loomis at first refuses,
he desperately wants

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:36.880
to find and stop Michael.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:38.038
This is where we really see his behavior

00:10:38.038 --> 00:10:40.483
cross over from a
concerned into obsessive.

00:10:40.483 --> 00:10:42.506
Michael Myers said essentially
become his life's work

00:10:42.506 --> 00:10:45.372
and he didn't have anything
or anyone else to go back to.

00:10:45.372 --> 00:10:47.830
He was ready to try to stop
Michael, no matter the cost.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.590
However, there was already a
state marshal waiting outside.

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:52.150
So Loomis had no choice but to be escorted

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:53.106
by him and Marion.

00:10:53.106 --> 00:10:55.200
I mean, I never understood
why he doesn't just try

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.150
to sneak out the back.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:58.040
I guess he just knows
that medicine is his thing

00:10:58.040 --> 00:10:59.300
and stealth is not.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.810
However, once in the police car,

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:02.547
he learns of a secret
government sealed document,

00:11:02.547 --> 00:11:04.468
which would change
everything he thought he knew

00:11:04.468 --> 00:11:06.004
about Michael's rampage.

00:11:06.004 --> 00:11:08.671
(ominous music)

00:11:10.804 --> 00:11:13.721
(fast eerie music)

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:17.000
On the car ride back into Smith's Grove,

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.091
Marion drops this bomb on Dr. Loomis.

00:11:19.091 --> 00:11:21.108
(eerie reel clicking)

00:11:21.108 --> 00:11:24.380
- There's a file on Michael
Myers that nobody knew about.

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:25.213
- I've seen everything.

00:11:25.213 --> 00:11:26.046
- No, no.

00:11:26.046 --> 00:11:27.546
It was hidden, sealed by the court

00:11:27.546 --> 00:11:30.041
after his parents were killed.

00:11:30.041 --> 00:11:32.905
Now after the Governor
heard what happened tonight,

00:11:32.905 --> 00:11:35.454
he authorized Dr. Rogers to open it.

00:11:35.454 --> 00:11:40.454
That girl, that Strode girl,
that's Michael Myers's sister.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:42.290
- Loomis has the revelation that Michael

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:44.760
is in Haddonfield to finish
what he started 15 years ago

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.140
by taking out the other sister.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:47.926
So he pleads with the marshal
to take him to the hospital

00:11:47.926 --> 00:11:50.270
where Laurie is being
kept, but to no avail.

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:51.113
So in a fit of desperation,

00:11:51.113 --> 00:11:53.280
he grabs his revolver
and to show he's serious,

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:55.450
fires a shot through the passenger window

00:11:55.450 --> 00:11:57.190
and demands to be taken to the hospital.

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:58.050
You can't just do that.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:11:59.958
I mean, where does he
think he is, LA county?

00:11:59.958 --> 00:12:02.348
Loomis's desperation is starting
to get the better of him.

00:12:02.348 --> 00:12:04.670
By threatening an officer
of the law at gunpoint,

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:05.503
he's basically declaring

00:12:05.503 --> 00:12:07.790
that he'll try to stop the
bogeyman of Haddonfield,

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:09.910
even if it means destroying himself.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.010
Dr. Samuel Loomis turned
from a by-the-book,

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:14.664
concerned psychiatrist to a
man overcome with obsession.

00:12:14.664 --> 00:12:16.084
I might normally compare his behavior

00:12:16.084 --> 00:12:18.150
against a medically recognized disorder

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:20.170
as I have for some other
characters that I've analyzed,

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:22.500
but as far as I can tell, he
doesn't really have a disorder.

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:24.190
He's just obsessed with stopping Michael,

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:25.210
and given what he's been through,

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:26.850
it's not impossible to blame him.

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.507
I think about every group project ever.

00:12:28.507 --> 00:12:31.050
Loomis has tried to convince
others and work with others

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:32.180
to prevent a disaster,

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:33.900
but eventually they all let him down

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:35.190
and he's going to do it himself,

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:36.810
even if this leads him down a dark road

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.749
of aggression and even committing crimes.

00:12:38.749 --> 00:12:40.541
It's probably a good thing too,

00:12:40.541 --> 00:12:42.850
because he arrives at Haddonfield Hospital

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:45.130
just in time to save Laurie
from Michael's wrath.

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:46.832
The state marshal is not so lucky.

00:12:46.832 --> 00:12:47.749
- [Sam] No!

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:51.882
(eerie music)

00:12:51.882 --> 00:12:54.140
- I guess Loomis is off the hook?

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:56.220
But also no, because he's once again

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:58.760
face-to-face with Michael,
and Michael is invincible.

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:01.010
He and Laurie run to try to
take cover in an operating room,

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:02.550
but Michael easily tears through the door

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:04.860
and stabs his doctor in the
stomach before turning his rage

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:06.847
against Laurie who managed to
get ahold of Loomis's revolver

00:13:06.847 --> 00:13:09.470
and shoot Michael in the eyes
to temporarily blind him.

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:11.419
Meanwhile, Loomis realizes it's
going to take something more

00:13:11.419 --> 00:13:14.170
than bullets or like a
cleverly placed trail

00:13:14.170 --> 00:13:16.245
of Reece's Pieces to stop
Michael and devises a plan

00:13:16.245 --> 00:13:18.920
to trap him by opening the
compressed gas canisters

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:20.821
in the room before saying this.

00:13:20.821 --> 00:13:22.890
- It's time Micheal.

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:24.740
- [Zac] And after giving
Laurie a moment to run for it,

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:25.920
he lights the place up,

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:28.640
potentially sacrificing himself
to put a stop to the evil

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:30.540
that inhabits the mind of his patient.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:33.330
On the morning of November
1st, the ambos role.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:34.940
That means ambulances came.

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:36.540
My mom heard it on a medical show once

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:37.530
and thought it was hilarious

00:13:37.530 --> 00:13:38.700
so I'm just going to go with it.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:41.340
Somehow, by some miracle, Dr. Sam Loomis

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:43.625
survived the massive explosion
at Haddonfield Hospital

00:13:43.625 --> 00:13:45.881
and the seemingly fatal
stab to his abdomen.

00:13:45.881 --> 00:13:48.170
He would live on with major
burns scars on his face

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:50.450
and walk with a limp needing to use a cane

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:51.520
for the rest of his life.

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:54.600
Not too bad for being blown up
as a 60 year old man, right?

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.580
Those must've been some real fast ambos.

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:58.599
However, as expected,
Michael isn't entirely

00:13:58.599 --> 00:14:01.520
out of the picture yet either,
but he does go into a coma,

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.270
allowing him to be
captured and placed back

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:04.740
into a psychiatric facility.

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:07.330
Despite Michael spending
the next 10 years in a coma,

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.483
Loomis is still obsessed
and still fears the evil

00:14:09.483 --> 00:14:10.511
that lurks within him.

00:14:10.511 --> 00:14:12.011
His new life's work is to prevent anyone

00:14:12.011 --> 00:14:13.830
from living through the Halloween night

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:14.706
that he and Laurie escaped.

00:14:14.706 --> 00:14:17.660
As more time passes, Michael
is seen as less and less

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:18.536
of a threat by his peers.

00:14:18.536 --> 00:14:20.346
Only he and Laurie know that one day,

00:14:20.346 --> 00:14:21.557
Michael will rise again.

00:14:21.557 --> 00:14:25.389
And then it's just him because
Laurie passes away in 1987,

00:14:25.389 --> 00:14:27.780
leaving behind a daughter named Jamie.

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:29.478
A year after her death,
Loomis is still fighting

00:14:29.478 --> 00:14:31.273
just as hard to keep Michael locked up.

00:14:31.273 --> 00:14:33.839
The staff actually go behind
his back to transfer Michael

00:14:33.839 --> 00:14:35.546
from the high security facility he's at,

00:14:35.546 --> 00:14:38.160
Ridgemont Federal Sanitarium,
back to Smith's Grove

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.586
on October 30th, 1988.

00:14:39.586 --> 00:14:41.547
Loomis immediately goes in to object

00:14:41.547 --> 00:14:43.410
when he finds out, and to his horror,

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:44.503
learns of an accident that occurred

00:14:44.503 --> 00:14:45.966
during the patient transport.

00:14:45.966 --> 00:14:47.960
Without another word, he
storms out of the room

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:49.799
to find his patient once
again and prevent a repeat

00:14:49.799 --> 00:14:52.450
of what happened 10 years
earlier to this day.

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:53.690
This time he suspects Michael

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.170
will be coming after
Laurie Strode's daughter,

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:57.014
Jamie Lloyd, the closest living relative.

00:14:57.014 --> 00:14:58.760
When Loomis sees the accident site,

00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:00.870
he's not too convinced
that it was an accident

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:02.331
and heads back to
Haddonfield for another round

00:15:02.331 --> 00:15:04.045
of serial killer hide-and-seek.

00:15:04.045 --> 00:15:05.530
- [Grace] Hide-and-Seek?

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:06.621
Are we really going to play that?

00:15:06.621 --> 00:15:08.230
- [Zac] No, not you.

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:09.063
Go away.

00:15:09.063 --> 00:15:10.430
Loomis stops at a gas station,

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:11.472
but upon further investigation,

00:15:11.472 --> 00:15:13.710
he finds more than he was expecting.

00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:15.736
For one, if you thought Loomis
was obsessed with Michael

00:15:15.736 --> 00:15:18.090
get a load of this gas
station diner owner.

00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:19.380
I think he's even more obsessed

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:20.629
with Regular Abraham Lincoln.

00:15:20.629 --> 00:15:22.655
Loomis finds the owner
tied up in metal chains

00:15:22.655 --> 00:15:24.903
and some woman on the floor
who also bit the dust.

00:15:24.903 --> 00:15:27.231
He tries to dial out for
help, but to his surprise,

00:15:27.231 --> 00:15:28.930
all of the phones had been broken.

00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:30.307
To be fair, Michael's
not going to use them,

00:15:30.307 --> 00:15:31.440
he doesn't talk.

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:34.137
But the biggest surprise
for Loomis is behind him.

00:15:34.137 --> 00:15:36.193
No, I mean the other direction.

00:15:36.193 --> 00:15:38.178
He turns and finds Michael
standing in the kitchen,

00:15:38.178 --> 00:15:39.608
just staring at him.

00:15:39.608 --> 00:15:42.189
Loomis pleads with him not
to return to Haddonfield.

00:15:42.189 --> 00:15:44.423
- If you want another victim, take me.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:48.916
But leave those people in peace.

00:15:48.916 --> 00:15:51.280
- With no response, Loomis
shoots off four rounds

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:53.840
from his gun but it's no
good, Michael vanishes.

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:55.160
Loomis runs outside to find him

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:57.030
when a truck smashes
through the garage doors.

00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:59.240
Loomis shoots are four
more rounds to no avail.

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:00.844
Michael intentionally
sideswipes the gas pump

00:16:00.844 --> 00:16:03.643
and the explosion and blows up
Loomis's car in the process.

00:16:03.643 --> 00:16:05.404
I always love how if you
look closely at the car,

00:16:05.404 --> 00:16:06.828
it just jumps off the ground.

00:16:06.828 --> 00:16:08.730
(eerie music and car explodes)

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.240
Dr. Sam probably didn't
find it so funny though.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.480
He's now stranded without a
way of catching up to Michael

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:15.478
and the hell that he's about
to unleash on Haddonfield.

00:16:15.478 --> 00:16:17.840
Loomis walks down the lonely
road and after being punked

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:20.241
by some kids, is picked up
by Reverend Jackson Sayer,

00:16:20.241 --> 00:16:21.985
who tells him that you can't kill evil.

00:16:21.985 --> 00:16:24.994
- [Sayer] It don't die like a man dies.

00:16:24.994 --> 00:16:26.887
- Loomis understands this all too well.

00:16:26.887 --> 00:16:29.694
He's been living with the
consequences of that since 1978.

00:16:29.694 --> 00:16:31.877
Sayer drops him at the
Haddonfield Police Station

00:16:31.877 --> 00:16:33.660
and he warns the new sheriff, Ben Meeker.

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:35.360
Just like practically everyone,

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:36.663
Meeker doesn't believe him at first.

00:16:36.663 --> 00:16:39.060
Imagine if people just listened to doctors

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:41.648
when they warn about dangerous things.

00:16:41.648 --> 00:16:43.653
After some debate, the
sheriff reluctantly declares

00:16:43.653 --> 00:16:45.834
a state of emergency and all
of Haddonfield's citizens

00:16:45.834 --> 00:16:47.743
are told to lock down
inside of their homes.

00:16:47.743 --> 00:16:49.745
Imagine if they actually listened.

00:16:49.745 --> 00:16:52.680
Dr. Loomis probably thinks
about Michael's attack pattern

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:53.968
10 years ago to make his next move.

00:16:53.968 --> 00:16:56.049
In '78, Michael went to his childhood home

00:16:56.049 --> 00:16:57.740
to try to find his sister Laurie,

00:16:57.740 --> 00:16:59.360
so this time Loomis suspects that he'll go

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:01.041
to the adoptive home of his niece, Jamie.

00:17:01.041 --> 00:17:03.424
There, he finds pictures of
Laurie scattered on the floor

00:17:03.424 --> 00:17:05.260
and the family dog.

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:07.199
Loomis is too late, but
he does learn that Michael

00:17:07.199 --> 00:17:10.215
is indeed repeating his 1978 rampage.

00:17:10.215 --> 00:17:11.593
Loomis and Meeker search the town

00:17:11.593 --> 00:17:12.842
and find Jamie trick or treating

00:17:12.842 --> 00:17:14.302
with her adoptive sister Rachel.

00:17:14.302 --> 00:17:16.240
They're picked up and
put in the squad car,

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:17.720
but find themselves immediately surrounded

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:20.824
by the very thing they were
supposed to be protected from.

00:17:20.824 --> 00:17:23.324
(eerie music)

00:17:25.232 --> 00:17:26.741
- Dear God.

00:17:26.741 --> 00:17:29.741
(suspenseful music)

00:17:31.572 --> 00:17:35.660
(fast beat eerie music)

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:37.287
- [Zac] After discovering
that some pranksters in town

00:17:37.287 --> 00:17:39.430
were doing a little Michael Myers cosplay,

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:41.514
and nearly shooting them,
Loomis and Sheriff Meeker

00:17:41.514 --> 00:17:42.880
returned to the police station

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:44.240
to find it completely destroyed,

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:46.122
with Michael also having
demoted one of the deputies

00:17:46.122 --> 00:17:49.330
to "Halloween decoration",
if you know what I mean.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:51.210
A good old group of Illinois boys show up

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:52.700
at the police station, demanding to know

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:54.210
what was going on in Haddonfield.

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:55.668
Loomis tells them that
Michael has returned,

00:17:55.668 --> 00:17:57.310
which Meeker isn't happy with,

00:17:57.310 --> 00:17:59.050
claiming that he just created a lynch mob.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.706
However, Loomis seems
undisturbed by this accusation.

00:18:01.706 --> 00:18:04.163
- You haven't got a police force.

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:07.498
These men may be the only defense you got.

00:18:07.498 --> 00:18:09.280
- [Zac] Being the only adult alive

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:11.940
that has witnessed the sheer
horror that is Michael,

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:13.790
it seems that he's willing
to just take whatever help

00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:14.623
he can get.

00:18:14.623 --> 00:18:18.092
He obviously did not realize
that cops do it by the book.

00:18:18.092 --> 00:18:20.531
I have no idea what that means still.

00:18:20.531 --> 00:18:22.406
They bring Jamie and Rachel
to the only safe place

00:18:22.406 --> 00:18:24.106
they have left, Sheriff Meeker's home,

00:18:24.106 --> 00:18:25.516
where with the help of Deputy Logan,

00:18:25.516 --> 00:18:27.780
they arm themselves
and board the place up.

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:28.878
Satisfied with Jamie's safety,

00:18:28.878 --> 00:18:30.335
Loomis goes back on the offensive

00:18:30.335 --> 00:18:32.657
and tries to return to
Jamie's house to find Michael.

00:18:32.657 --> 00:18:34.868
He doesn't find him, but
he does later that night,

00:18:34.868 --> 00:18:37.370
run back into Jamie as
she is running from him

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:39.410
and decides to take her to
the schoolhouse for safety.

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:41.920
A school may have actually
been considered safe back then,

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:44.210
I don't know, but I guess this
school would be considered

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:46.183
an exception because Michael
is already there waiting

00:18:46.183 --> 00:18:49.108
for them and throws Loomis
through a glass door.

00:18:49.108 --> 00:18:50.990
(glass shattering)

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:51.823
Loomis is pretty metal.

00:18:51.823 --> 00:18:53.750
I mean, he's been stabbed, blown up,

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:55.090
and now thrown through a door.

00:18:55.090 --> 00:18:57.390
Seems like he's just as
hard to kill as Michael is.

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:58.901
Loomis is present later on when the police

00:18:58.901 --> 00:19:01.510
and the Illinois boys all
shoot Michael down at once,

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:02.968
sending him into a
well, and interestingly,

00:19:02.968 --> 00:19:05.800
he seems to believe that Michael
is actually dead this time,

00:19:05.800 --> 00:19:07.780
despite years of evidence
that Michael's death

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:09.348
is simply not a possibility.

00:19:09.348 --> 00:19:11.753
- Micheal Meyers is in Hell.

00:19:11.753 --> 00:19:13.837
Buried where he belongs.

00:19:13.837 --> 00:19:16.610
- It seems out of character
for Loomis to be that naive.

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:17.443
Doesn't it?

00:19:17.443 --> 00:19:19.330
My take is that he was
about 70 at this point

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:20.972
and he probably didn't think
you'd be around if Michael

00:19:20.972 --> 00:19:23.104
came back after another 10 years or so.

00:19:23.104 --> 00:19:25.114
Almost like he needed to
believe that Michael was dead

00:19:25.114 --> 00:19:26.367
so he could die in peace.

00:19:26.367 --> 00:19:28.666
Obviously, the real reason is
that director Dwight Little,

00:19:28.666 --> 00:19:30.930
didn't really want to make
another "Halloween" movie,

00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:33.787
but this is a video about
Loomis, not Dwight Little.

00:19:33.787 --> 00:19:36.580
(sad music, distorted)

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:38.630
Dr. Loomis returns home
with Jamie and her family

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:39.730
to help them settle back in,

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:41.240
but after hearing a chilling scream,

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.696
Loomis rushes to the
stairway to find Jamie

00:19:42.696 --> 00:19:44.520
holding a pair of scissors.

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:46.181
Loomis cannot believe what he sees.

00:19:46.181 --> 00:19:49.000
The evil he's spent the last
25 years trying to vanquish

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.250
is now logged into the
body of the one girl

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.509
that he was able to save.

00:19:52.509 --> 00:19:53.757
To put this into perspective,

00:19:53.757 --> 00:19:55.219
this is like playing a whole game,

00:19:55.219 --> 00:19:57.710
but then your file gets deleted at 99%.

00:19:57.710 --> 00:19:59.740
Loomis's psyche begins to break.

00:19:59.740 --> 00:20:02.010
The terror of the idea that
the evil had just latched

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:04.180
onto another soul is too
much for him to bear.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:05.308
And he raises his gun to shoot,

00:20:05.308 --> 00:20:07.504
but not before being
stopped by Sheriff Meeker.

00:20:07.504 --> 00:20:09.760
However, the circumstances
are not quite as bad

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:11.120
as they first seemed.

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:13.150
Over the next year, Jamie
seems to get control

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:14.920
of the evil connection she now has.

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:16.736
She is now the newest
patient of Dr. Loomis,

00:20:16.736 --> 00:20:19.190
but she doesn't become
an empty soulless shape

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:20.110
like Michael had.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.911
She does, however, go
mute due to the trauma

00:20:21.911 --> 00:20:24.110
of the year before and
suffers from what seem to be

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:25.630
terrors and seizures in the nights,

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:27.616
but Loomis seems to know that
there's more to it than that.

00:20:27.616 --> 00:20:28.750
For his own sake,

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:30.440
it's probably a good thing
that he's able to work

00:20:30.440 --> 00:20:32.940
with Jamie, because he now has
something to live for again.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:34.311
But because he's so jaded now,

00:20:34.311 --> 00:20:36.906
it often comes off as
kind of scary for her.

00:20:36.906 --> 00:20:38.530
Loomis comes and checks on Jamie one day

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:40.020
during her stay at the facility

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:41.900
while Rachel and her
friend Tina are visiting.

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:43.381
A brick smashes through
the window with a note

00:20:43.381 --> 00:20:46.100
attached reading, "The
evil child must die!"

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:47.560
Loomis believes that people of Haddonfield

00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:48.780
are afraid of Jamie because they think

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:50.074
that she's following
in Michael's footsteps.

00:20:50.074 --> 00:20:53.480
On October 31st, 1989, one a
year into his care for her,

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:55.614
Jamie drew something that
caught Loomis's attention,

00:20:55.614 --> 00:20:57.871
a horrific drawing of the family dog Max.

00:20:57.871 --> 00:21:00.450
I would not want to be a dog
in Haddonfield in late October.

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:02.234
Loomis called the family's
home to check on Max,

00:21:02.234 --> 00:21:04.397
because he had discovered
that Jamie could sense things.

00:21:04.397 --> 00:21:06.650
He aggressively demanded
that she write down

00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:08.143
whatever she knew.

00:21:08.143 --> 00:21:09.685
- Write, write, write!

00:21:09.685 --> 00:21:12.807
For me, this is the point
of no return for Loomis.

00:21:12.807 --> 00:21:13.836
He has good intentions,

00:21:13.836 --> 00:21:15.737
but he doesn't treat Jamie
with the same patience

00:21:15.737 --> 00:21:17.166
that he gave Michael early on.

00:21:17.166 --> 00:21:19.746
Jamie soon suffers another
seizure, which convinces Loomis

00:21:19.746 --> 00:21:21.630
that she's mentally linked to Michael.

00:21:21.630 --> 00:21:23.270
He tells Sheriff Meeker
about how he believes

00:21:23.270 --> 00:21:24.800
that Michael is still alive.

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:26.817
- Hell would not have him.

00:21:26.817 --> 00:21:28.253
- [Zac] But the sheriff is
called away to the cemetery

00:21:28.253 --> 00:21:30.248
and so Loomis returns to
try to get more answers

00:21:30.248 --> 00:21:31.114
out of Jamie.

00:21:31.114 --> 00:21:33.571
(equipment clatters)

00:21:33.571 --> 00:21:36.380
- What about your stepmother, Jamie?

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:37.213
- Harry!

00:21:37.213 --> 00:21:39.150
Harry, did you put your
name in the Goblet of Fire!

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:41.002
He then tells Jamie of
his trip to the cemetery

00:21:41.002 --> 00:21:42.831
where supposedly someone
had dug up the coffin

00:21:42.831 --> 00:21:44.325
of a nine year old girl.

00:21:44.325 --> 00:21:47.700
- What do you think he's
going to do with that?

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:49.050
- Whoa, man.

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:50.660
He also tries searching
the Meyers house again,

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:53.090
but honestly, what is he going
to do to him at this point?

00:21:53.090 --> 00:21:54.584
He shot him several times, blew him up,

00:21:54.584 --> 00:21:55.839
loaded him with bullets again,

00:21:55.839 --> 00:21:57.533
and yet Michael still lives on.

00:21:57.533 --> 00:21:58.366
For these reasons,

00:21:58.366 --> 00:22:00.570
I don't think he was
there to find Michael.

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:01.943
I think he was there to set a trap,

00:22:01.943 --> 00:22:04.822
which would come into play
later that Halloween night.

00:22:04.822 --> 00:22:07.489
(ominous music)

00:22:10.485 --> 00:22:12.985
(eerie music)

00:22:14.550 --> 00:22:17.060
Dr. Loomis decides to stay
by Jamie's side that evening

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:18.760
as she attends her school's costume party.

00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:20.220
It's here that she has another vision.

00:22:20.220 --> 00:22:21.610
Thanks to her connection with her uncle,

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:23.003
which helps them figure
out that Tina Williams

00:22:23.003 --> 00:22:25.250
was in danger near Dale's
gas station across town.

00:22:25.250 --> 00:22:27.140
And Loomis gets Sheriff
Meeker on the phone

00:22:27.140 --> 00:22:27.973
to help save her.

00:22:27.973 --> 00:22:29.760
Tina returns to the
clinic to comfort Jamie

00:22:29.760 --> 00:22:30.926
for a short period of time but decides

00:22:30.926 --> 00:22:32.878
to attend a Halloween
party later that evening.

00:22:32.878 --> 00:22:33.921
Loomis begs her to stay,

00:22:33.921 --> 00:22:35.790
thinking that she's still
going to be in danger,

00:22:35.790 --> 00:22:37.229
but Tina doesn't believe
him and blames him

00:22:37.229 --> 00:22:38.319
for filling Jamie's head

00:22:38.319 --> 00:22:40.400
with all of these boogeyman stories.

00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:42.270
The interaction shows
that he's become seen

00:22:42.270 --> 00:22:43.490
by the younger people in town

00:22:43.490 --> 00:22:44.484
as more of a crazy old man

00:22:44.484 --> 00:22:47.590
than an experienced Michael
Myers veteran and survivor.

00:22:47.590 --> 00:22:49.700
Loomis instructs the local
police to follow her.

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:51.955
However, Jamie sees that Tina
is going to be in danger again

00:22:51.955 --> 00:22:54.640
and sneaks out to try to warn her herself.

00:22:54.640 --> 00:22:56.084
- Jamie's not in her room.

00:22:56.084 --> 00:22:58.175
She's nowhere in sight.

00:22:58.175 --> 00:22:59.676
(child laughs)

00:22:59.676 --> 00:23:00.549
- [Girl] Hey!

00:23:00.549 --> 00:23:01.840
(child screams)

00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:02.673
- [Meeker] Loomis!

00:23:02.673 --> 00:23:03.810
What the hell are you doing?
- [Male Speaker] Take it easy.

00:23:03.810 --> 00:23:04.760
- My thoughts, exactly.

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:06.191
The guy is just out of control.

00:23:06.191 --> 00:23:08.712
However, he still keeps
finding ways to be helpful

00:23:08.712 --> 00:23:10.410
as he helps the police find Jamie

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:12.220
who had escaped with their
classmate, Billy Hill,

00:23:12.220 --> 00:23:13.053
near an old barn.

00:23:13.053 --> 00:23:14.632
They were not in time to save Tina,

00:23:14.632 --> 00:23:16.659
but Jamie and Billy
are escorted to safety.

00:23:16.659 --> 00:23:18.610
Jamie is gaining some of her voice back

00:23:18.610 --> 00:23:20.480
and she asks if Loomis will
be able to kill Michael

00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:21.710
to which he replies.

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:23.150
- I think so.

00:23:23.150 --> 00:23:24.124
- For some reason,

00:23:24.124 --> 00:23:27.121
even though nothing in this
26 year span should lead him

00:23:27.121 --> 00:23:28.860
to believe that Michael is mortal.

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:31.100
On the bright side for them,
this causes Jamie to agree

00:23:31.100 --> 00:23:32.838
to help Loomis and the
police by using her visions

00:23:32.838 --> 00:23:34.414
to help locate and catch Michael.

00:23:34.414 --> 00:23:36.790
As the ambos and police
officers leave the scene,

00:23:36.790 --> 00:23:38.033
Loomis approaches the edge of the forest

00:23:38.033 --> 00:23:39.736
and yells into the trees at Michael,

00:23:39.736 --> 00:23:41.914
claiming that his rage
will destroy him someday,

00:23:41.914 --> 00:23:44.540
that killing everyone
will not make it go away.

00:23:44.540 --> 00:23:45.988
He instructs Michael to go home

00:23:45.988 --> 00:23:48.240
where Loomis and Jamie
will be waiting for him.

00:23:48.240 --> 00:23:50.470
Sure enough, they set up
Jamie in Judith's old room

00:23:50.470 --> 00:23:51.740
as the police surround the house

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:53.923
and wait for Haddonfield's
silent killer to approach.

00:23:53.923 --> 00:23:56.340
Loomis is waiting in the hall
when he's called into the room

00:23:56.340 --> 00:23:57.510
because Jamie's having another one

00:23:57.510 --> 00:23:59.210
of her psychic connection episodes.

00:23:59.210 --> 00:24:00.958
This time, it appears that
Billy is the one in danger,

00:24:00.958 --> 00:24:03.589
though I guess you could argue
that this was all a diversion

00:24:03.589 --> 00:24:05.164
based on what happens in that next.

00:24:05.164 --> 00:24:07.454
Loomis radios the sheriff
and tells him that Michael

00:24:07.454 --> 00:24:08.930
is at the Children's Clinic.

00:24:08.930 --> 00:24:10.543
So Meeker sends all of his officers there,

00:24:10.543 --> 00:24:12.870
leaving the outside of
the house unguarded.

00:24:12.870 --> 00:24:14.689
It seems like this was
Loomis his plan all along.

00:24:14.689 --> 00:24:16.732
It could be that he figures
Michael will not show up

00:24:16.732 --> 00:24:18.740
if the police are all
around or maybe he thought

00:24:18.740 --> 00:24:20.636
that with fewer people,
there'll be fewer casualties.

00:24:20.636 --> 00:24:23.200
Plus, this kind of allows
him to operate the way

00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:25.530
that he wants to, which
as we'll see shortly,

00:24:25.530 --> 00:24:27.383
is probably not something that
anyone on the police force

00:24:27.383 --> 00:24:28.806
would have approved of.

00:24:28.806 --> 00:24:30.799
He tells the one remaining
officer to stay with Jamie

00:24:30.799 --> 00:24:33.130
as he descends towards the
main level of the house

00:24:33.130 --> 00:24:34.390
where Michael is coming in

00:24:34.390 --> 00:24:36.292
and they meet face-to-face once again.

00:24:36.292 --> 00:24:38.368
Knowing he's here for
Jamie, Loomis informs him

00:24:38.368 --> 00:24:41.100
that he believes Jamie can
stop the rage inside of him.

00:24:41.100 --> 00:24:42.630
He reminds him of how he used to be

00:24:42.630 --> 00:24:44.040
before the rage engulfed him.

00:24:44.040 --> 00:24:45.077
He's trying to break through to Michael

00:24:45.077 --> 00:24:46.157
on a more human level,

00:24:46.157 --> 00:24:48.580
a side of him that the doctor
had long thought to be dead.

00:24:48.580 --> 00:24:50.615
Why does he suddenly think
he can reach some semblance

00:24:50.615 --> 00:24:52.773
of humanity buried inside
of his former patient?

00:24:52.773 --> 00:24:54.095
It's because of Jamie.

00:24:54.095 --> 00:24:56.473
Jamie was supposedly overcome
by the same evil that affected

00:24:56.473 --> 00:24:57.650
that affected Michael,

00:24:57.650 --> 00:24:59.130
but she was able to overcome it

00:24:59.130 --> 00:25:00.479
and go back to being a good person.

00:25:00.479 --> 00:25:03.151
He tries to take Michael's
knife away from him gently

00:25:03.151 --> 00:25:04.980
until Michael cuts him across the stomach

00:25:04.980 --> 00:25:06.772
and throws him through a railing.

00:25:06.772 --> 00:25:08.662
(Loomis gasps and screams)

00:25:08.662 --> 00:25:11.412
(glass shatters)

00:25:12.738 --> 00:25:14.590
(Loomis yells)

00:25:14.590 --> 00:25:15.870
Michael follows the sound of Jamie

00:25:15.870 --> 00:25:17.410
and the officer upstairs trying to escape.

00:25:17.410 --> 00:25:19.100
And after Jamie is
almost killed by Michael,

00:25:19.100 --> 00:25:20.711
about a hundred times,
she runs back downstairs

00:25:20.711 --> 00:25:22.667
and finds Loomis there to comfort her,

00:25:22.667 --> 00:25:24.544
but things take a turn for the worse.

00:25:24.544 --> 00:25:26.449
Instead of running away
like normal people,

00:25:26.449 --> 00:25:28.958
Loomis decides to lure and
taunt Michael with Jamie,

00:25:28.958 --> 00:25:31.770
using her as bait at
the end of the stairs.

00:25:31.770 --> 00:25:33.027
- [Loomis] You want her!

00:25:33.873 --> 00:25:35.670
- [Jamie] No!
- Here she is!

00:25:35.670 --> 00:25:37.538
- This is almost
definitely the worst thing

00:25:37.538 --> 00:25:39.771
that he's ever done because
judging by her reaction,

00:25:39.771 --> 00:25:42.750
Jamie had no idea that she
was going to be used as bait

00:25:42.750 --> 00:25:45.129
like this in such a close
encounter with her masked stalker.

00:25:45.129 --> 00:25:47.705
- [ColossalIsCrazy] This is the
face of the clinically insane.

00:25:47.705 --> 00:25:51.384
If you see this man do not engage him.

00:25:51.384 --> 00:25:54.193
- [Sam] Micheal, let's play a game.

00:25:54.193 --> 00:25:57.870
- Yep, he is officially crossed
into Jigsaw territory now.

00:25:57.870 --> 00:25:59.570
- Catch the little girl.

00:25:59.570 --> 00:26:02.518
- Okay, so he's not actually
giving her up to him at least,

00:26:02.518 --> 00:26:04.299
I guess that's slightly redeeming.

00:26:04.299 --> 00:26:06.110
When Michael reaches
the middle of the room,

00:26:06.110 --> 00:26:08.820
Loomis pulls a rope, releasing
a net made with heavy chains.

00:26:08.820 --> 00:26:10.666
He also loads him up with
darts from a tranquilizer gun,

00:26:10.666 --> 00:26:12.093
and in a moment of madness,

00:26:12.093 --> 00:26:14.850
just savagely beats him
with this wooden board.

00:26:14.850 --> 00:26:15.832
- [Sam] Die!

00:26:15.832 --> 00:26:16.734
Die!

00:26:16.734 --> 00:26:18.117
Die!

00:26:18.117 --> 00:26:19.783
Die, Michael!

00:26:22.230 --> 00:26:23.357
- Not sure that's going to do a lot,

00:26:23.357 --> 00:26:24.680
but it probably felt good.

00:26:24.680 --> 00:26:29.250
- [Chris] I didn't know where I
was for a minute, felt good though.

00:26:29.250 --> 00:26:31.230
- The police show up and
place Michael in holding,

00:26:31.230 --> 00:26:33.709
which is glossed over, but it's
a huge milestone for Loomis.

00:26:33.709 --> 00:26:36.350
People are finally seeing
Michael the way that he sees him

00:26:36.350 --> 00:26:38.070
and they're willing to
put him in an actual jail

00:26:38.070 --> 00:26:40.430
rather than dumping him in
another psychiatric facility.

00:26:40.430 --> 00:26:42.628
The plan is to transfer him
to a maximum security facility

00:26:42.628 --> 00:26:46.200
where he would stay until death
or in his case just forever.

00:26:46.200 --> 00:26:48.720
Unfortunately for Haddonfield
and its police force,

00:26:48.720 --> 00:26:50.749
forever ends up not even
being more than a night

00:26:50.749 --> 00:26:53.080
because a mysterious character
in a black trench coat

00:26:53.080 --> 00:26:55.550
shows up, takes out the
entire police station

00:26:55.550 --> 00:26:57.060
and frees Michael Myers.

00:26:57.060 --> 00:26:58.850
I compared Dr. Loomis to Jigsaw earlier,

00:26:58.850 --> 00:27:00.096
so I guess this guy is Hoffman.

00:27:00.096 --> 00:27:01.401
- Game over.

00:27:01.401 --> 00:27:03.533
- Michael was free to
exercise his immortality

00:27:03.533 --> 00:27:05.820
against the people of
Haddonfield once more.

00:27:05.820 --> 00:27:07.646
But Dr. Loomis's health
would finally get the better

00:27:07.646 --> 00:27:10.534
of him as he suffered a
stroke not long after.

00:27:10.534 --> 00:27:13.034
(eerie music)

00:27:15.496 --> 00:27:18.996
(suspenseful piano music)

00:27:20.020 --> 00:27:21.846
I imagine that Halloween in 1989

00:27:21.846 --> 00:27:24.390
was the biggest rollercoaster
that Samuel Loomis

00:27:24.390 --> 00:27:25.223
ever went through.

00:27:25.223 --> 00:27:26.991
He had finally found
Michael, captured him,

00:27:26.991 --> 00:27:30.270
only for him to be released
by another powerful evildoer.

00:27:30.270 --> 00:27:31.700
Based on the information we have,

00:27:31.700 --> 00:27:33.890
Loomis suffered a stroke
sometime after this.

00:27:33.890 --> 00:27:36.100
But I like to imagine that
it was the same night.

00:27:36.100 --> 00:27:37.510
Right when he found out
that Michael had escaped,

00:27:37.510 --> 00:27:39.805
his brain basically freaked
out and he ends up realizing

00:27:39.805 --> 00:27:41.849
that he can't go on like this anymore.

00:27:41.849 --> 00:27:43.250
For the better of his health,

00:27:43.250 --> 00:27:45.254
he retired from his position
at Smith's Grove Sanitarium

00:27:45.254 --> 00:27:46.710
and moved to a secluded lifestyle

00:27:46.710 --> 00:27:48.640
in a cabin in rural Illinois.

00:27:48.640 --> 00:27:51.077
He also got surgery to remove
the burn scars from his face.

00:27:51.077 --> 00:27:53.800
Everything was peaceful
for the next six years

00:27:53.800 --> 00:27:55.419
until he got a visit from an old friend

00:27:55.419 --> 00:27:59.490
on October 30th, 1995, his
old boss, Dr. Terrance Wynn,

00:27:59.490 --> 00:28:00.610
comes in to see him

00:28:00.610 --> 00:28:01.612
on that dark rainy night,

00:28:01.612 --> 00:28:03.446
Wynn had come to celebrate
his own retirement

00:28:03.446 --> 00:28:04.621
and wants to convince Loomis

00:28:04.621 --> 00:28:07.021
to go back as chief
administrator of Smith's Grove.

00:28:07.021 --> 00:28:08.149
It's during this discussion

00:28:08.149 --> 00:28:10.593
that Loomis recognizes a
familiar voice on the radio

00:28:10.593 --> 00:28:11.426
calling for help.

00:28:11.426 --> 00:28:13.838
That voice belongs to
Jamie, now 15 years old,

00:28:13.838 --> 00:28:16.056
and her body is discovered
mutilated the next morning,

00:28:16.056 --> 00:28:17.563
Halloween 1995.

00:28:17.563 --> 00:28:19.481
Loomis knows that the
nightmare has returned.

00:28:19.481 --> 00:28:21.744
And Michael Myers was back for round six.

00:28:21.744 --> 00:28:24.128
Despite the fact that he's
already on borrowed time

00:28:24.128 --> 00:28:25.700
and being in his mid seventies

00:28:25.700 --> 00:28:28.050
and having endured a handful
of life-threatening scenarios,

00:28:28.050 --> 00:28:29.360
he just can't turn a cold shoulder

00:28:29.360 --> 00:28:30.696
to the city of Haddonfield.

00:28:30.696 --> 00:28:33.730
Even now, they still don't seem
to have any respect for him,

00:28:33.730 --> 00:28:35.053
despite all he's been through for them.

00:28:35.053 --> 00:28:36.930
- It's been quiet here for six years

00:28:36.930 --> 00:28:38.752
and that's the way it's going to stay.

00:28:38.752 --> 00:28:41.360
The last thing I need
now is you going around

00:28:41.360 --> 00:28:42.870
spouting off ghost stories.

00:28:42.870 --> 00:28:45.620
- Loomis quickly retorts that
Michael Myers is his business.

00:28:45.620 --> 00:28:47.707
He's now a part of the
legend of Michael Myers.

00:28:47.707 --> 00:28:50.317
The townspeople almost see him
as synonymous with Michael,

00:28:50.317 --> 00:28:51.807
as if he's some kind of warning sign

00:28:51.807 --> 00:28:53.208
that the boogeyman is back.

00:28:53.208 --> 00:28:55.500
Loomis and Wynn go to the
hospital to visit Jamie,

00:28:55.500 --> 00:28:57.840
when he's approached by an
even older familiar face.

00:28:57.840 --> 00:28:59.490
This is Tommy Doyle, the little boy

00:28:59.490 --> 00:29:00.519
that Laurie Strode was babysitting

00:29:00.519 --> 00:29:02.892
on that fateful Halloween night in 1978.

00:29:02.892 --> 00:29:04.868
Tommy starts to tell him
about other relatives

00:29:04.868 --> 00:29:06.498
in the Strode family that are now living

00:29:06.498 --> 00:29:08.100
in Michael's old house,

00:29:08.100 --> 00:29:09.830
but he's rushed out of
the hospital by security

00:29:09.830 --> 00:29:11.250
before he can tell the whole story.

00:29:11.250 --> 00:29:12.756
Tommy tells him to meet
him at the campus rally

00:29:12.756 --> 00:29:14.095
at nine that night and Loomis knows

00:29:14.095 --> 00:29:15.900
that he'll have to prepare himself

00:29:15.900 --> 00:29:17.764
to face his old patient one last time.

00:29:17.764 --> 00:29:20.640
As per tradition, he pays a
visit to Michael's old house,

00:29:20.640 --> 00:29:22.620
but it's new residents
aren't home when he arrived.

00:29:22.620 --> 00:29:23.999
So he just makes like
a video game character

00:29:23.999 --> 00:29:25.382
and lets himself inside.

00:29:25.382 --> 00:29:27.299
Eventually he meets
these Strode matriarch,

00:29:27.299 --> 00:29:29.550
Debra Strode, and warns
her of his suspicion

00:29:29.550 --> 00:29:30.594
of Michael's immediate return.

00:29:30.594 --> 00:29:33.170
He urges her and her family
to immediately leave town.

00:29:33.170 --> 00:29:34.544
When he gets back to the hospital,

00:29:34.544 --> 00:29:37.058
he learns that Jamie was
offed the previous night.

00:29:37.058 --> 00:29:38.454
He confronts Jamie's doctor,

00:29:38.454 --> 00:29:40.170
outraged, and in a great amount of pain

00:29:40.170 --> 00:29:41.360
because of Jamie's passing.

00:29:41.360 --> 00:29:43.935
Remember, Jamie was essentially
Dr. Loomis's greatest work.

00:29:43.935 --> 00:29:45.260
He was able to save her

00:29:45.260 --> 00:29:46.900
from becoming the next Michael Meyers.

00:29:46.900 --> 00:29:47.736
The conversation does yield

00:29:47.736 --> 00:29:49.950
an interesting piece
of information though.

00:29:49.950 --> 00:29:50.810
If there's some kind of a law

00:29:50.810 --> 00:29:52.660
about sharing a patient's
medical information,

00:29:52.660 --> 00:29:53.868
the doctor ignores it and reveals

00:29:53.868 --> 00:29:55.948
that he found placental
fluids in Jamie's body,

00:29:55.948 --> 00:29:58.489
meaning she had given birth
about 24 hours before.

00:29:58.489 --> 00:30:00.900
Only they did not know where the baby was.

00:30:00.900 --> 00:30:03.090
Loomis, on the other hand, thinks he does.

00:30:03.090 --> 00:30:05.284
He meets Tommy at the campus
rally looking to talk further,

00:30:05.284 --> 00:30:07.588
but first they discover
another Meyers casualty.

00:30:07.588 --> 00:30:10.440
This time, the body of radio
personality, Barry Simms.

00:30:10.440 --> 00:30:11.845
Loomis and Tommy returned
to the boarding house

00:30:11.845 --> 00:30:13.650
that Tommy is staying at across the street

00:30:13.650 --> 00:30:15.471
from the old Meyers house but
they discover that the baby,

00:30:15.471 --> 00:30:18.120
which Tommy is named
Steven, is now missing.

00:30:18.120 --> 00:30:19.816
There were also two other
Strodes taking cover

00:30:19.816 --> 00:30:22.256
in Tommy's room, Kara
Strode and her son, Danny.

00:30:22.256 --> 00:30:24.550
These are the adoptive
cousins of Laurie Strode,

00:30:24.550 --> 00:30:26.548
and they're also now missing,
but they're soon discovered

00:30:26.548 --> 00:30:28.410
when Michael chases them to the front door

00:30:28.410 --> 00:30:29.243
and Tommy lets them in.

00:30:29.243 --> 00:30:32.290
Tommy asks Loomis 'who else
knew about the baby Steven?'

00:30:32.290 --> 00:30:34.480
Which leads him to
having a big realization.

00:30:34.480 --> 00:30:36.559
(eerie reel clicking)

00:30:36.559 --> 00:30:38.390
- Who else knew I had the baby?

00:30:38.390 --> 00:30:39.223
- No one.

00:30:39.223 --> 00:30:40.056
- [Tommy] No.

00:30:40.056 --> 00:30:41.890
There had to be someone else.

00:30:41.890 --> 00:30:42.723
Who knew?

00:30:42.723 --> 00:30:45.780
- Nobody knew expect me and...

00:30:45.780 --> 00:30:47.650
- They turned to the
living room and see Danny,

00:30:47.650 --> 00:30:50.230
sitting on the lap of the
mysterious black trench coat man

00:30:50.230 --> 00:30:52.020
who helped free Michael in 1989,

00:30:52.020 --> 00:30:52.853
who turns out to be none other

00:30:52.853 --> 00:30:55.132
than the retiring Smith's
Grove administrator,

00:30:55.132 --> 00:30:56.490
Dr. Terrance Wynn.

00:30:56.490 --> 00:30:58.249
Loomis discovers that Wynn
is part of an organization

00:30:58.249 --> 00:31:00.764
called the "Cult of Thorn"
who worships the demon Thorn,

00:31:00.764 --> 00:31:03.813
the same evil that possessed
Michael Myers since 1963,

00:31:03.813 --> 00:31:05.489
and can not leave his body until he kills

00:31:05.489 --> 00:31:07.704
the last remaining member
of Michael's family.

00:31:07.704 --> 00:31:09.950
This explains Michael's entire life.

00:31:09.950 --> 00:31:11.500
Since that first dreaded Halloween,

00:31:11.500 --> 00:31:13.664
which was now 32 years ago.

00:31:13.664 --> 00:31:15.750
Dr. Loomis takes Tommy
Doyle back to Smith's Grove

00:31:15.750 --> 00:31:17.680
one last time and asked
Tommy to wait in the hall

00:31:17.680 --> 00:31:19.240
as he confronts Wynn, who invites him

00:31:19.240 --> 00:31:20.145
to join the Cult of Thorn.

00:31:20.145 --> 00:31:22.130
Loomis isn't having any of that though,

00:31:22.130 --> 00:31:23.198
and is prepared to shoot Dr. Wynn,

00:31:23.198 --> 00:31:25.130
but one of the cult
members sneaks up on him

00:31:25.130 --> 00:31:25.963
and knocks him out.

00:31:25.963 --> 00:31:28.270
(Loomis groans in pain)

00:31:28.270 --> 00:31:29.571
He wakes up around the time that Tommy

00:31:29.571 --> 00:31:31.692
has rescued Kara,
Steven, and Danny Strode,

00:31:31.692 --> 00:31:33.310
and helps them get away from Michael

00:31:33.310 --> 00:31:34.690
by shooting the controls for the door

00:31:34.690 --> 00:31:36.417
and hailing an elevator
for Kara and the kids.

00:31:36.417 --> 00:31:38.173
Tommy catches up with
them and invites Loomis

00:31:38.173 --> 00:31:39.980
to flee the hospital with them.

00:31:39.980 --> 00:31:42.253
But Loomis's decision goes
back to the decision he made

00:31:42.253 --> 00:31:44.678
when all of this Cult
of Thorn business began.

00:31:44.678 --> 00:31:45.810
He was happily retired

00:31:45.810 --> 00:31:48.570
when he discovered
Michael's return in 1995

00:31:48.570 --> 00:31:50.480
And he made the decision
to come back to Haddonfield

00:31:50.480 --> 00:31:52.415
to try to stop Michael one last time.

00:31:52.415 --> 00:31:54.531
He knew he didn't have
much gas left in the tank

00:31:54.531 --> 00:31:57.144
and he was never planning on
walking away with his own life.

00:31:57.144 --> 00:31:59.650
We never see exactly what his fate is,

00:31:59.650 --> 00:32:01.296
but his story ends on this shot

00:32:01.296 --> 00:32:03.380
where Michael has shed
his mask on the floor

00:32:03.380 --> 00:32:04.213
next to a syringe

00:32:04.213 --> 00:32:06.346
and we hear Loomis cry out one final time

00:32:06.346 --> 00:32:07.851
before his story ends.

00:32:07.851 --> 00:32:10.601
(Loomis screams)

00:32:13.570 --> 00:32:15.360
I've always interpreted
this ending to mean

00:32:15.360 --> 00:32:16.772
that Loomis eventually lost his life

00:32:16.772 --> 00:32:18.308
doing what he dedicated it to,

00:32:18.308 --> 00:32:21.300
trying to hunt down his most
infamous psychiatric patient.

00:32:21.300 --> 00:32:23.909
Technically speaking, it's
a very ambiguous ending.

00:32:23.909 --> 00:32:25.690
You could say that both of their fates

00:32:25.690 --> 00:32:28.090
at the end of this timeline
will always be unknown.

00:32:28.090 --> 00:32:29.017
The reason for my interpretation

00:32:29.017 --> 00:32:30.982
has more to do with the context behind it.

00:32:30.982 --> 00:32:33.350
The original ending known,
as the "Producer's Cut,"

00:32:33.350 --> 00:32:35.140
shows Loomis going back to Smith's Grove

00:32:35.140 --> 00:32:36.710
and discovering what he thinks is Michael,

00:32:36.710 --> 00:32:38.020
but turns out to be Dr. Wynn

00:32:38.020 --> 00:32:40.190
with the iconic Michael Myers
mask placed over his face,

00:32:40.190 --> 00:32:42.100
leaving the story open
for another chapter.

00:32:42.100 --> 00:32:43.942
But sadly, the actor Donald Pleasance

00:32:43.942 --> 00:32:45.604
passed away shortly after filming.

00:32:45.604 --> 00:32:47.900
So the ending was reworked
for the theatrical cut,

00:32:47.900 --> 00:32:48.979
which is technically canon,

00:32:48.979 --> 00:32:50.707
and gives us a more of a proper conclusion

00:32:50.707 --> 00:32:51.722
to Loomis's story.

00:32:51.722 --> 00:32:53.347
We see Dr. Samuel Loomis turned

00:32:53.347 --> 00:32:54.711
from a clinical psychologist,

00:32:54.711 --> 00:32:56.371
treating mentally distressed children,

00:32:56.371 --> 00:32:58.122
to a man obsessed with the destruction

00:32:58.122 --> 00:32:59.760
of one of his patients.

00:32:59.760 --> 00:33:01.709
While that doesn't sound like
the most noble of characters

00:33:01.709 --> 00:33:03.306
on the surface, when you break him down,

00:33:03.306 --> 00:33:05.488
you discover that he
puts the care of others

00:33:05.488 --> 00:33:06.528
first in his heart,

00:33:06.528 --> 00:33:08.328
and even before himself,

00:33:08.328 --> 00:33:10.219
he's a selfless man giving
his time and his energy

00:33:10.219 --> 00:33:11.681
to protect the town of Haddonfield

00:33:11.681 --> 00:33:13.190
and the Strode family line.

00:33:13.190 --> 00:33:15.500
And he continues to do so,
even though none of the people

00:33:15.500 --> 00:33:17.241
he saves end up respecting him.

00:33:17.241 --> 00:33:19.373
His later years were corrupted
by his growing obsession

00:33:19.373 --> 00:33:20.791
with stopping his adversary,

00:33:20.791 --> 00:33:22.456
which only worsened his reputation

00:33:22.456 --> 00:33:25.310
but he kept on fighting
right down to the very end.

00:33:25.310 --> 00:33:27.210
Let me know in the comments
what Halloween character

00:33:27.210 --> 00:33:29.604
you'd like to see me cover
next on "Horror History."

00:33:29.604 --> 00:33:30.953
There are a ton of options.

00:33:30.953 --> 00:33:32.870
For example, the Rob
Zombie timeline version

00:33:32.870 --> 00:33:35.239
of Dr. Loomis is a different
character that I could analyze.

00:33:35.239 --> 00:33:36.948
That leaves us with like four Laurie's,

00:33:36.948 --> 00:33:39.882
four Michael's, and probably
two or three Tommy's.

00:33:39.882 --> 00:33:41.710
We could be at this for a while.

00:33:41.710 --> 00:33:43.290
So let me know who you really want to see.

00:33:43.290 --> 00:33:44.223
You'll find all of those videos

00:33:44.223 --> 00:33:45.642
in the playlist on the left.

00:33:45.642 --> 00:33:48.150
Remember to subscribe to CZSWorld

00:33:48.150 --> 00:33:49.580
for new horrors every week,

00:33:49.580 --> 00:33:51.900
ring the death bell for all notifications.

00:33:51.900 --> 00:33:56.226
And I'll see you in the next
one, assuming we both survive.

00:33:56.226 --> 00:33:59.393
(upbeat techno music)

